{"message":"I can’t file the Evergreen disputes yet because the dispute form requires a definite answer about whether you currently have the physical card. Please check and answer **yes** or **no** for card ending 9251. “Unknown” is acceptable for PIN compromise, but not for card possession.

The TechWorld dispute also cannot be filed without the complete discovery date in MM/DD/YYYY format. Since the transaction occurred on 10/04/2025, a discovery date of 01/12/2025 would be before the transaction and outside the 60-day filing window; I can’t assume what year or date you intended.

I have not filed any disputes yet. I also need to check the Green Fee-Free account’s existing open-dispute limit before filing all three Green-card disputes, because Green Fee-Free is an Entry Tier account with a maximum of two open disputes per checking account."}

{"message":"Yes—there is a limit, but it does not prevent you from filing all three Green-card disputes indefinitely. The Green Fee-Free account is Entry Tier, allowing up to 2 open disputes at a time. I checked your records and found 1 existing open dispute on the Evergreen account; Evergreen is Premium Tier, allowing up to 4 open disputes, so there is room for the two Evergreen disputes you identified.

Before I can file either Evergreen dispute, please check whether you currently have the physical card ending in 9251 and answer **yes** or **no**. This single answer can apply to both the Phoenix Kitchen Supply and Rho-Bank ATM deposit disputes. Your PIN status for both will be recorded as **unknown**.

I have not filed any new disputes yet."}
